{
  "id": "lesson-linq-034",
  "slug": "conversion-operators",
  "moduleSlug": "conversion-generation-operators",
  "title": "Conversion Operators",
  "description": "Learn to convert between different collection types using LINQ conversion operators.",
  "order": 34,
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedMinutes": 15,
  "tags": [
    "linq",
    "conversion",
    "asEnumerable",
    "asQueryable",
    "cast",
    "toArray",
    "toList"
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Conversion operators in LINQ convert the type of elements in a sequence (collection). There are three types:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "**As operators** (AsEnumerable, AsQueryable) — Cast to IEnumerable<T> or IQueryable<T>",
          "**To operators** (ToArray, ToList, ToDictionary, ToLookup) — Force execution and convert",
          "**Casting operators** (Cast, OfType) — Convert non-generic to generic collections"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "AsEnumerable & AsQueryable"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "The `AsEnumerable` and `AsQueryable` methods cast or convert a source object to `IEnumerable<T>` or `IQueryable<T>` respectively."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "AsEnumerable & AsQueryable",
        "content": "Converting to IEnumerable and IQueryable",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "Student[] studentArray = {\n    new Student() { StudentID = 1, StudentName = \"John\", Age = 18 },\n    new Student() { StudentID = 2, StudentName = \"Steve\", Age = 21 }\n};\n\n// AsEnumerable converts to IEnumerable<T>\nIEnumerable<Student> enumerable = studentArray.AsEnumerable();\n\n// AsQueryable converts to IQueryable<T>\nIQueryable<Student> queryable = studentArray.AsQueryable();"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Cast Operator"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "The `Cast<T>()` method converts a non-generic collection to a generic collection."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Cast Example",
        "content": "Converting non-generic to generic collection",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "ArrayList mixedList = new ArrayList() { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 };\n\nIEnumerable<int> intList = mixedList.Cast<int>();\n\n// Result: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "To Operators"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "The `To` operators force query execution and convert the result to a specific collection type."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "ToArray & ToList",
        "content": "Converting to array and list",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "IList<string> strList = new List<string>() { \"One\", \"Two\", \"Three\" };\n\nstring[] strArray = strList.ToArray();\nIList<string> list = strArray.ToList();"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "ToDictionary",
        "content": "Converting to dictionary",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "IList<Student> studentList = new List<Student>() {\n    new Student() { StudentID = 1, StudentName = \"John\", Age = 18 },\n    new Student() { StudentID = 2, StudentName = \"Steve\", Age = 21 },\n    new Student() { StudentID = 3, StudentName = \"Bill\", Age = 18 }\n};\n\n// Convert to dictionary with StudentID as key\nIDictionary<int, Student> studentDict = studentList.ToDictionary(s => s.StudentID);\n\n// Access by key\nStudent john = studentDict[1];"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "data": {
        "variant": "info",
        "title": "Forcing Query Execution",
        "text": "To operators force immediate execution of deferred queries. This is important when working with remote data sources like databases."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "summary-box",
      "data": {
        "title": "Key Takeaways",
        "points": [
          "AsEnumerable/AsQueryable cast to IEnumerable/IQueryable",
          "Cast converts non-generic to generic collections",
          "To operators force query execution and convert types",
          "ToArray, ToList, ToDictionary are commonly used"
        ],
        "takeaway": "Continue to the next lesson to learn about generation operators."
      }
    }
  ],
  "relatedLessons": [
    "generation-operators",
