  "tags": [
    "linq",
    "contains",
    "quantifiers"
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "The `Contains` operator checks whether a specified element exists in a collection and returns a boolean."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "The `Contains()` extension method has two overloads:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Contains Method Signatures",
        "content": "The two overloads of Contains",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "public static bool Contains<TSource>(this IEnumerable<TSource> source, TSource value);\n\npublic static bool Contains<TSource>(this IEnumerable<TSource> source, TSource value, IEqualityComparer<TSource> comparer);"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Contains with Primitive Types",
        "content": "Checking if a value exists in a collection",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "IList<int> intList = new List<int>() { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 };\nbool result = intList.Contains(10);  // returns false"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Contains with Complex Types"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "For custom classes, `Contains` compares references by default, not values. This means it may return `false` even if an object with the same values exists:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Contains with Complex Types (Default)",
        "content": "Reference comparison with custom classes",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "IList<Student> studentList = new List<Student>() {\n    new Student() { StudentID = 1, StudentName = \"John\", Age = 18 },\n    new Student() { StudentID = 2, StudentName = \"Steve\", Age = 15 },\n    new Student() { StudentID = 3, StudentName = \"Bill\", Age = 25 },\n    new Student() { StudentID = 4, StudentName = \"Ram\", Age = 20 },\n    new Student() { StudentID = 5, StudentName = \"Ron\", Age = 19 }\n};\n\nStudent std = new Student() { StudentID = 3, StudentName = \"Bill\" };\nbool result = studentList.Contains(std);  // returns false (different reference)"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "To compare values of custom classes, implement `IEqualityComparer<T>`:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Contains with Custom Comparer",
        "content": "Value comparison with IEqualityComparer",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "class StudentComparer : IEqualityComparer<Student>\n{\n    public bool Equals(Student x, Student y)\n    {\n        if (x.StudentID == y.StudentID &&\n            x.StudentName.ToLower() == y.StudentName.ToLower())\n            return true;\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    public int GetHashCode(Student obj)\n    {\n        return obj.GetHashCode();\n    }\n}\n\nStudent std = new Student() { StudentID = 3, StudentName = \"Bill\" };\nbool result = studentList.Contains(std, new StudentComparer());  // returns true"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "data": {
        "variant": "warning",
        "title": "Not Supported in Query Syntax",
        "text": "The Contains operator is not supported in C# or VB.NET query syntax."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "summary-box",
      "data": {
        "title": "Key Takeaways",
        "points": [
