{
  "id": "lesson-linq-003",
  "slug": "linq-api-in-net",
  "moduleSlug": "getting-started-linq",
  "title": "LINQ API in .NET",
  "description": "Explore the LINQ API architecture, including the Enumerable and Queryable classes, and how they enable LINQ queries.",
  "order": 3,
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedMinutes": 15,
  "tags": [
    "linq",
    "api",
    "ienumerable",
    "iqueryable",
    "enumerable",
    "queryable"
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "We can write LINQ queries for classes that implement the `IEnumerable<T>` or `IQueryable<T>` interface. The `System.Linq` namespace includes the classes and interfaces required for LINQ queries."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "data": {
        "variant": "info",
        "title": "System.Linq Namespace",
        "text": "The `System.Linq` namespace is included by default when you add a new class in Visual Studio. It contains all the core types needed for LINQ queries."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "How LINQ Works with Interfaces"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "LINQ queries use extension methods for classes that implement `IEnumerable` or `IQueryable` interfaces. The `Enumerable` and `Queryable` are two static classes that contain extension methods to write LINQ queries."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "mermaid",
      "data": {
        "id": "linq-api-architecture",
        "caption": "LINQ API architecture showing Enumerable and Queryable classes",
        "definition": "graph TD\n    A[System.Linq Namespace] --> B[Enumerable Class]\n    A --> C[Queryable Class]\n    B --> D[IEnumerable&lt;T&gt;]\n    C --> E[IQueryable&lt;T&gt;]\n    D --> F[In-Memory Collections]\n    E --> G[Remote Data Sources]\n    F --> H[Lists, Arrays, Dictionaries]\n    G --> I[Databases, Web Services]"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Enumerable Class"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "The `Enumerable` class includes extension methods for classes that implement the `IEnumerable<T>` interface. All built-in collection classes in .NET implement `IEnumerable<T>`, so we can write LINQ queries to retrieve data from these collections."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Use `Enumerable` extension methods when working with in-memory collections like:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Arrays (`int[]`, `string[]`, etc.)",
          "Generic collections (`List<T>`, `Dictionary<K,V>`)",
          "Other in-memory data structures"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Using Enumerable Extension Methods",
        "content": "LINQ queries on in-memory collections use Enumerable",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "using System.Linq;\n\nList<int> numbers = new List<int> { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 };\n\n// Uses Enumerable.Where() extension method\nvar evenNumbers = numbers.Where(n => n % 2 == 0);\n\n// Uses Enumerable.Select() extension method\nvar doubled = numbers.Select(n => n * 2);"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Queryable Class"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "The `Queryable` class includes extension methods for classes that implement the `IQueryable<T>` interface. The `IQueryable<T>` interface provides querying capabilities against a specific data source where the type of the data is known."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "For example, Entity Framework implements `IQueryable<T>` to support LINQ queries with underlying databases such as MS SQL Server."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Queryable with Entity Framework",
        "content": "LINQ queries on databases use Queryable",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "using System.Linq;\n\n// Entity Framework DbContext\nusing (var context = new SchoolContext())\n{\n    // Uses Queryable.Where() - translated to SQL\n    var students = context.Students\n        .Where(s => s.Age > 18)\n        .ToList();\n}"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Third-Party Data Providers"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "There are APIs available to access third-party data. For example, **LINQ to Amazon** provides the ability to use LINQ with Amazon web services to search for books and other items. This is achieved by implementing the `IQueryable` interface for Amazon."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "IEnumerable<T>",
            "definition": "An interface that allows iteration over a collection. All LINQ to Objects queries work on this interface."
          },
          {
            "term": "IQueryable<T>",
            "definition": "An interface that provides querying capabilities for remote data sources. Queries are translated to the native query language (e.g., SQL)."
          },
          {
            "term": "Enumerable",
            "definition": "A static class that contains extension methods for IEnumerable<T> types, used for in-memory queries."
          },
          {
            "term": "Queryable",
            "definition": "A static class that contains extension methods for IQueryable<T> types, used for remote data source queries."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "summary-box",
      "data": {
        "title": "Key Takeaways",
        "points": [
          "LINQ queries work with IEnumerable<T> and IQueryable<T> interfaces",
          "Enumerable class provides extension methods for in-memory collections",
          "Queryable class provides extension methods for remote data sources",
          "Third-party providers can implement IQueryable for LINQ support"
        ],
        "takeaway": "Continue to the next lesson to see the complete LINQ learning roadmap."
      }
    }
  ],
  "relatedLessons": [
    "what-is-linq",
    "why-linq"
  ]
}
